From 35be43a4e4aa5261d4bc49a6dcacec120a64f5d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: l4h <z@univalence.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:16:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] smp: read remote call arguments only for a pending call

handleIPI() passed ipi->remoteCall and ipi->args to handleRemoteCall(),
which then checks that this core's ipi flag is set, ignoring spurious
IPIs. The arguments were thus read before the flag. A core that handled
a call from the lock's wait loop can take that call's hardware IPI late,
while the next call is being set up: it may read the previous call's
operation and arguments, then see the flag of the next call, and run the
old operation in the new round.

Under load (Linux guests unmapping memory on 4 cores) this both skipped
TLB and paging-structure invalidations, corrupting user memory, and
re-ran old invalidations on VSpace roots that had since been reused,
loading a CR3 without kernel mappings: a triple fault.

Check the flag, with acquire ordering, before reading the call.
---
 src/smp/ipi.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/smp/ipi.c b/src/smp/ipi.c
index 538f91323..63606b523 100644
--- a/src/smp/ipi.c
+++ b/src/smp/ipi.c
@@ -123,6 +123,16 @@ void handleIPI(irq_t irq, bool_t irqPath)
     ipi_state_t *ipi = &big_kernel_lock.ipi;
 
     if (IRQT_TO_IRQ(irq) == irq_remote_call_ipi) {
+        /* The call and its arguments belong to this core only while its
+         * ipi flag is set, and are only visible once the flag is (the
+         * sender sets it with a release store after writing them). The
+         * hardware IPI of a call already handled from the lock's wait loop
+         * can arrive while the next call is being set up: reading the
+         * arguments before the flag would run the previous call's
+         * operation, with possibly stale arguments, in the next round. */
+        if (!clh_is_ipi_pending(getCurrentCPUIndex())) {
+            return;
+        }
         handleRemoteCall(ipi->remoteCall, ipi->args[0], ipi->args[1], ipi->args[2], irqPath);
     } else if (IRQT_TO_IRQ(irq) == irq_reschedule_ipi) {
         rescheduleRequired();
